# Workspace-root .dockerignore.
#
# Every Dockerfile in this repo is built with the WORKSPACE ROOT as its build
# context, so the builder stage can see bun.lock, every member package.json,
# and the packages/* sources that apps link via `workspace:*`. This file keeps
# that context small — and keeps `.env*` out of image layers.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the builder.
**/node_modules

# Build outputs / caches — regenerated inside the builder.
**/dist
**/storybook-static
**/build
**/out
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Foreign lockfiles (bun.lock at the root IS shipped — that's what
# `bun install --frozen-lockfile` reads).
**/package-lock.json
**/yarn.lock
**/pnpm-lock.yaml

# Environments — never bake into an image.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Nix / direnv — host-only.
.direnv
flake.nix
flake.lock
.envrc

# Logs
**/*.log
**/logs

# Editor / OS noise
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# Git
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Docs (kept on the host)
**/*.md
!README.md

# Claude / AI tooling — local-only
.claude
**/CLAUDE.md

# Docker artefacts (referenced with -f, no need inside the context)
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.*
**/.dockerignore

# Azure pipeline definitions — consumed by Azure DevOps, not the builder
**/azure-release*.yaml
**/docker-build*.yml
